      "writtenOn": "2017-07-27T17:03:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s possible to use hybrid properties in sql to give you this information in the driver instead of doing it manually here. We do this across the identity backend with the different user types.\n\nWhat you can do is define a hybrid property called tags on the sql driver for projects. When you call project.tags you can tell it to list all tags associated to the project by having it query a separate table [0].\n\nI haven\u0027t benchmarked this approach, but I\u0027d guess that it\u0027s probably more efficient than carrying this logic in python.\n\n[0] https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/c3b5d2d77b029880521912e43ad963f9b0c5bf99/keystone/identity/backends/sql_model.py#L71",
