      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: this method is raising validation errors, but i\u0027m not sure what\u0027s being validated or when. Instead, one way to decouple this, is to have the method return True or False answer the question \"is the current tag limit at capacity?\". Then the methods in the API or Manager, are responsible for raising the ValidationErrors\n\n  def _is_project_over_tag_limit(self, project_id):\n  \"\"\"Check the capacity of the current tags associate to a project.\"\"\"\n      return len(self.driver.list_project_tags(project_id)) \u003e\u003d MAX_PROJECT_TAG_COUNT\n\nthen we can do things like:\n\n  def create_project_tag(self, project_id, tag_name):\n      if is_project_over_tag_limit(project_id):\n          raise exception.ValidationError(...)",
